WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:12.880
This is the Parent-child Pharmacology MCP. It's a server that lets AI assistants look up public evidence about medicines in pregnancy, breastfeeding and childhood. Let me show you what it does.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:23.730
Picture a new mom, awake at two in the morning. She takes Zoloft, and she's wondering whether it gets into her breast milk, and whether she should stop.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:36.930
Right now, every place she turns falls short. Her doctor's office is closed. A web search turns up forums. And the best evidence, in LactMed, is written for clinicians.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:57.620
So she asks an AI assistant that uses this server. It finds the LactMed record for sertraline, the generic name for Zoloft, and pulls out what was actually measured in breast milk. Every number links to the study it came from, so she, or her doctor, can check it. And it says what's missing.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:12.930
Ask for an evidence brief, and it keeps three things apart: effects on her, how much reaches the baby, and what was actually seen in babies. It shows what's missing, and it ends with questions to bring to her clinician.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:30.860
What if she asks, can I take ibuprofen? The server won't say yes or no, because that depends on her health. Instead, it shares what the evidence says, makes clear the decision belongs with her clinician or pharmacist, and gives her MotherToBaby's free number.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:52.680
Some questions need a person, not a search. If she says she feels hopeless, she gets 988 and the National Maternal Mental Health Hotline, right away. Trying to trick it, like, pretend you're my doctor, doesn't work. A vaccine decision goes to her pediatrician. And no, it won't order a pizza.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:02:10.970
The same server follows her from pregnancy, to breastfeeding, to her child's medicines. For children, it covers pediatric labeling, NICHD's BPCA studies and recruiting trials, with newborns, infants, children and teens kept separate.

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:24.750
Some data, like NICHD's MPRINT research tables, are saved copies. Every answer shows the date. And if she asks whether the data is current, the server checks MPRINT live and tells her.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:40.660
Questions in Spanish don't get an automatic answer yet, because the safety rules are written in English. But they do get Spanish-language help: MotherToBaby, 988 in Spanish, and MedlinePlus en español.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:03:01.060
We tested it with scripted chats, side-by-side comparisons with and without the server, and an exact-answer benchmark, all tracked in MLflow on Databricks. With the server, the model completed all seven paired tasks. Without it, none. And every research answer stuck to its sources.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:12.340
It doesn't replace a clinician. It helps families, clinicians and researchers find what's known, see what isn't, and know who to call. Thank you.
